      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yep, after further testing, the trick i use is to open and close vrchat right as steam vr boots up, then reebooting vrchat so that the steam vr overlay stops working. This brought a significant boost in FPS and had no memory leak whatsoever! My internet was fast and I could actually load everyone's avatar on The Great Pug, something almost impossible before.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
